1. Create the Pod
kubectl apply -f multi-container-pod.yaml

2. Check Pod
kubectl get pods

You should see:

NAME                   READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE
multi-container-pod    2/2     Running   0          20s

2/2 means both containers are running.

3. Check both containers
kubectl describe pod multi-container-pod

4. Check Nginx logs
kubectl logs multi-container-pod -c nginx

5. Check Ubuntu logs
kubectl logs multi-container-pod -c ubuntu

6. Enter the Nginx container
kubectl exec -it multi-container-pod -c nginx -- /bin/bash

7. Enter the Ubuntu container
kubectl exec -it multi-container-pod -c ubuntu -- /bin/bash
Important concept

A multi-container Pod means multiple containers run inside the same Pod and share:

Same IP address
Same network
Same localhost
Can share volumes

Example architecture:

             Multi-Container Pod
        ┌──────────────────────────┐
        │                          │
        │   Nginx Container        │
        │   Port: 80               │
        │                          │
        │   Ubuntu Container       │
        │   Background process     │
        │                          │
        └──────────────────────────┘
                    │
               Same Pod IP